  "final_message": "The key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nWhen I read `audit.py`, line 11 showed up redacted, so I ran the code to get the real value:\n\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")`.\n2. `write_audit` sets `key = [REDACTED:SECRET]\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`.\n3. `AUDIT_PREFIX` is `\"AUD\"` in `config.py`, so the result is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nRunning `checkout(\"7781\")` produced a log dict containing only that key. `decoy_metrics.py` builds keys the same way, but it writes to a metrics dict with the `MET` prefix and never touches the audit log. `decoy_cache.py` doesn't touch it either.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
